    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Four perspectives, one shared curiosity</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">Build <span>&amp; beyond.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">We’re computer science students exploring what thoughtful software can do—and how AI is changing the way we make it. Meet the people, ideas, and questions behind our work.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="hero-note">
        <strong>Our starting point</strong>
        <p>Useful software takes more than fast code: it takes curiosity, good judgement, and care for the systems—and people—on the other side.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="team" aria-labelledby="team-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Meet the people</p>
          <h2 id="team-title">Different paths.<br>Shared momentum.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>From systems and security to AI and full-stack building, our experiences shape the questions we bring to software engineering.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="team-grid">
        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:akshay.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Akshay">
          <h3>Akshay</h3>
          <p class="study">MSc Computer Science</p>
          <p class="bio">Akshay Pradeep Kumar studies computer science at master’s level. Running and travelling keep him curious beyond his studies, and he has recently started to love cooking. He sees AI as a way for developers to complete tasks faster and believes people may reach new heights in technology with its help. For him, the next era of software engineering will reward creativity in deciding what to make, not just the ability to code it.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: Akshay has recently started to love cooking.</em></p>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <strong>Interests</strong>
            <p>Running · Travelling · Cooking</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <strong>Looking ahead</strong>
            <p>He expects software engineering to become more about creative problem selection and making than coding alone.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 We’re teaching machines to code so we can finally spend our time arguing about what to build.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:leman.png}}" alt="Photo of Leman">
          <h3>Leman</h3>
          <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, 5th semester, Universität Paderborn · B.Sc., Ahsanullah University of Science and Technology, Bangladesh</p>
          <p class="bio">Leman is a fifth-semester M.Sc. student at Universität Paderborn and earned a B.Sc. from Ahsanullah University of Science and Technology in Bangladesh. Data science, video games, and books are among Leman’s interests. People often describe Leman as a bit introverted—a description Leman disagrees with. Leman sees AI as helpful for quickly handling menial setup and repetitive tasks, while also recognising its effects on the job sector.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: People say Leman is a bit introverted, but Leman doesn’t agree.</em></p>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <strong>Interests</strong>
            <p>Data science · Video gaming · Reading books</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <strong>Looking ahead</strong>
            <p>Leman expects a shift from line-by-line coding toward system design. AI will take on boilerplate and more of the path from building an app to shipping it; people who can guide it across whole systems will be ahead.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 AI won’t replace good software developers. Better developers are who that can use AI tools better.</p>
        </article>

